<title>GREECE: Bank of Greece drains 150bln drs at avg 12.14pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Greece drains 150bln drs at avg 12.14pct.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of Greece drained 150 billion drachmas of 14-day funds at a weighted average interest rate of 12.12 percent in today's money market tender, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>The lowest accepted interest rate stood at 11.85 percent and the highest interest rate at 12.24 percent, it added. --Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
